        "project": "/tmp/m3-crew",
        "culture": "We work on Jhin itself, in the checkout /tmp/m3-crew (branch m3-run-crew), which both nodes share. Read AGENTS.md first and follow it: docs/map.md before building, the plan that owns the area, docs/lore/. Every change is a reviewed slice; commit on m3-run-crew with Conventional Commits, one commit per item, and never push. Decisions are numbered D1565–D1574 only, recorded in docs/plans/agents.md under M3 (\"Decisions (M3)\"), and the item moves out of agents.md#deferred when it lands. Run heavy commands (vitest, vp test, typecheck, builds, playwright) through ~/.t3/jhin-heavy, and only for the files you touched. Ask before you guess; a public id (AGENTS.md rule 8) or a choice of product behaviour is the owner's to decide, so escalate it.",
        "agents": {
          "lead": {
            "title": "Lead",
            "role": "Talks to the owner, plans missions in waves and runs them with the orchestrator",
